PERSONNEL -- SHINOBI REGISTRATION RECORD (SPECIMEN FORMAT)
Kazekage Office, Identity Division

Every shinobi of the Hidden Sand is entered in the village register upon
graduation. This specimen shows the recorded fields; individual files are sealed.

Registered fields:
- Name and Academy graduation cycle
- Assigned rank (Genin / Chunin / Jonin) and current standing
- Primary chakra nature (predominantly Wind in Sunagakure) and known affinities
- Specialization (e.g., Puppet Brigade, wind-user, medical corps, reconnaissance)
- Squad assignment and reporting jonin
- Headband issuance number (cross-ref identity file)

Sample entries by way of format:
- Temari -- Jonin -- Wind nature -- battle-fan specialist -- Sand Siblings unit.
- Kankuro -- Jonin -- Puppet Brigade -- multiple registered puppets.
- Gaara -- Kazekage -- sand manipulation, One-Tail host -- office of the Kage.

Registration is the root record binding a shinobi to the village. Desertion
voids standing and flags the file to the missing-nin watch. Sealed.
